# Netlify's CDN does not serve files that live inside a dot-prefixed
# directory (like .well-known/) even when they're present in the deployed
# bundle -- a rewrite that targets another path *inside* that same
# dot-directory doesn't help, since the destination is just as unreachable.
# The fix: keep the real file at a normal, non-hidden path and rewrite the
# dot-path request to it. This is what makes Android's
# /.well-known/assetlinks.json (TWA/App Links verification) actually work.
/.well-known/assetlinks.json  /assetlinks.json  200!
